<LegalPage
  appName="Hustlrr"
  docTitle="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Hustlrr handles your data: what the app collects, why, who processes it, and your rights under the GDPR."
  canonicalUrl="https://rubenspessoa.dev/hustlrr/privacy/"
  effectiveDate="July 22, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what data the Hustlrr app for iPhone, iPad, and Mac collects, why, who
    processes it, and the rights you have. Hustlrr works without an account, your conversations
    are stored on your own device, and we do not sell or share your data for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho
    <br />
    UNESCO-Esplanade 8/55, 8020 Graz, Austria
    <br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a> for full legal details.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

  <h3>Your conversations</h3>
  <p>
    When you send a message, the content of that conversation &mdash; your text, uploaded
    documents, and text transcribed from voice input &mdash; is sent through our servers to the
    AI provider behind the model you selected (currently OpenAI and Anthropic) solely to generate
    the response. Under our API agreements, this content is not used to train AI models. Our
    servers relay your messages and do not keep a copy of your conversations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your chat history is stored on your device and, if you use iCloud, synced through your own
    private iCloud storage, which we cannot access.
  </p>

  <h3>App verification</h3>
  <p>
    To keep bots and abusers away from the AI features, every request to our servers carries a
    token from Firebase App Check (Google) that verifies it comes from a genuine, unmodified copy
    of Hustlrr on a real device. These checks rely on device attestation services operated by
    Apple and Google. No account, email, or password is involved.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    Subscriptions are sold and billed by Apple through the App Store. We never see your payment
    details. RevenueCat (USA) processes your App Store transaction status together with an
    anonymous identifier so the app knows whether your subscription is active.
  </p>

  <h3>Usage analytics</h3>
  <p>
    We use TelemetryDeck (Germany), a privacy-focused analytics service, to understand how the app
    is used: features used and events such as a completed chat. TelemetryDeck anonymizes
    identifiers before storage and cannot identify you personally. We use this under our
    legitimate interest in improving the product.
  </p>

  <h3>Crash and error reports</h3>
  <p>
    The app uses Sentry (USA) to collect crash and error reports: technical details such as device
    model, OS version, and stack traces that help us find and fix problems.
  </p>

  <h3>Server logs and usage counters</h3>
  <p>
    Our servers keep short-lived technical logs and usage counters (keyed to anonymous
    identifiers) for rate limiting and abuse prevention. These expire automatically. We do not log
    the content of your conversations.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR we process data based on: <strong>performance of a contract</strong> (relaying
    your messages to AI providers and providing your subscription),
    <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (product analytics, crash reporting, abuse prevention).
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Apple (USA): App Store distribution, payments, device services, iCloud</li>
    <li>Google Firebase (USA): server infrastructure and app verification</li>
    <li>OpenAI (USA) and Anthropic (USA): generating responses to your messages</li>
    <li>RevenueCat (USA): subscription status</li>
    <li>TelemetryDeck (Germany): anonymized product analytics</li>
    <li>Sentry (USA): crash and error reporting</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where providers are located in the USA, transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework
    and/or Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Conversations: not retained on our servers (relayed and discarded)</li>
    <li>Rate-limit and usage counters: short-lived, expire automatically</li>
    <li>
      Analytics and crash data: per the retention settings of the respective tool, kept only as
      long as needed for the purposes above
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access, rectify, delete, restrict, or receive a copy of your data, and
    to object to processing based on legitimate interest. Because we hold no account for you,
    exercising these rights works by email: write to
    <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>. You also have the
    right to complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (
    <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dsb.gv.at</a>) or
    your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Hustlrr is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will update it here with a new effective date. Material changes
    will be highlighted in the app.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
